-- Migration 0097: FK leading-column indexes (round-9 remediation)
--
-- Auditor finding: foreign-key columns without a leading-column index force
-- sequential scans on every join, cascade delete, and FK validation. This
-- migration was generated by scanning drizzle/0000-0034 + drizzle/migrations/
-- 0019-0096 for REFERENCES constraints and cross-checking every existing
-- CREATE INDEX leading column. Tables the audit named (complaint_events,
-- scan_findings, settlement_instalments, whistleblower_messages,
-- bundle_access_log, payment_installments, receipts, refund_requests,
-- payment_rrr_codes) were verified to ALREADY have leading-column indexes;
-- the list below is the verified remainder.
--
-- Idempotent: every statement uses IF NOT EXISTS. Plain (non-concurrent)
-- indexes so the file runs inside the migration runner's transaction; the
-- affected tables are operational-scale, not bulk-event-scale.

-- NOTE (round-10 fix): idx_adverse_media_entity_matches_item_id was removed
-- from this file — adverse_media_entity_matches is created later by
-- 0112_adverse_media.sql, so indexing it here broke fresh-database applies.
-- The index now lives in 0123_fk_indexes_adverse_media_fixforward.sql.

